claude <claude@p7x.dev> writes:

> A pass always picked its own message, so whatever ran it could not say
> which message that pass was for, and so could not check afterwards
> that this message was answered. A driver that runs one pass per
> message has to know which message each pass is for.
>
> The skill now takes a notmuch id. Without one it still falls back to
> the oldest inbox message, so /process-email by hand works as before.
> A message that is no longer in the inbox ends the pass without
> writing, because someone has already answered or archived it.

Simplify this so an argument is required.

We are moving logic out of inference and into determinism. So wherever
we can do that, we should.
